t><idPurp>This layer has been produced to support--inasmuch as this is feasible--routing applications that must coincide with the geometry of the Road Inventory. All overlapping features have been eliminated, and segmentation has been adjusted to run from at-grade intersection to at-grade intersection, with a consequent distortion of regular Road Inventory attributes. Although the attributes are indicative of conditions found along the segments, they are not necessarily true along their whole lengths, and this layer should NOT BE USED for summary reporting on attributes.</idPurp><searchKeys><keyword>freeways</keyword><keyword>median</keyword><keyword>road inventory</keyword><keyword>functional classification</keyword><keyword>functional class</keyword><keyword>roads</keyword><keyword>routes</keyword><keyword>lanes</keyword><keyword>local roads</keyword><keyword>mileage</keyword><keyword>traffic count</keyword><keyword>collectors</keyword><keyword>speed limit</keyword><keyword>major streets</keyword><keyword>ADT</keyword><keyword>sidewalks</keyword><keyword>major roads</keyword><keyword>highways</keyword><keyword>streets</keyword><keyword>Chapter 90</keyword></searchKeys><idAbs>&lt;DIV STYLE="text-align:Left;"&gt;&lt;DIV&gt;&lt;DIV&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;The Massachusetts Department of Transportation Highway Division Road Inventory contains the spatial linework for all the public--and a good portion of the private--roadways and shared-use paths in Massachusetts, along with attributes covering the roadway classification, ownership, physical conditions, traffic volumes, pavement conditions, highway performance monitoring information, and more. This layer originated with the routes underlying the Road Inventory, from which overlapping sections were removed. The remaining route sections were broken at at-grade intersections and attributed using the Road Inventory attributes applicable to the midpoint of the segments.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/DI